      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The conformal field theory framework for two-dimensional critical phenomena gave statistical physics a remarkably powerful and general way to classify and calculate universal behavior. Its conceptual reach and lasting use make it a strong prize-level contribution.",
        "attribution": "The seminal work is closely associated with Belavin, A. Zamolodchikov, and Polyakov, whose joint contribution is appropriately recognized here.",
        "maturity": "The framework has been established for decades and repeatedly validated through its consequences for critical systems.",
        "uncertainties": [
