        "Mehran Kardar",
        "Yi-Cheng Zhang"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The KPZ theory identified a universal scaling description for stochastic growth, with influence extending well beyond its original setting. Its combination of a simple mechanism and broad predictive reach is compelling.",
        "attribution": "Kardar and Zhang are central to the foundational theory. Takeuchi's experimental confirmation is valuable, though the theoretical discovery is the principal prize contribution described here.",
        "maturity": "The universality class has extensive theoretical and experimental support, including precise modern tests.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The ballot also names experimental confirmation; how much credit to assign to that distinct contribution is not fully specified."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 3,
