        "Antoine Georges",
        "Dieter Vollhardt",
        "Gabriel Kotliar"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Dynamical mean-field theory made strongly correlated electron systems tractable through a disciplined local approximation, opening a major route from microscopic models to material behavior. It is a deep and broadly useful theoretical advance.",
        "attribution": "Georges, Vollhardt, and Kotliar are appropriately associated with the development and systematization of the theory.",
        "maturity": "The method has been extensively developed and applied over several decades, with clear successes and known limits.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The proposed scope should distinguish the original formulation from later extensions and from parallel work on related impurity methods."
        ]
      }
    },
