      "rank": 4,
      "ballot_id": "B054",
      "proposed_laureates": [
        "Andrea J. Liu",
        "Sidney R. Nagel"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The jamming transition organized disparate observations about disordered materials around a common physical picture of rigidity and arrest. Its cross-system reach and enduring role in soft-matter physics are substantial.",
        "attribution": "Liu and Nagel are strongly identified with formulating and developing the jamming framework, though the experimental and theoretical foundations span a wider community.",
        "maturity": "The field has matured through extensive work on granular materials, foams, and glasses, while active questions remain about universality and the precise relation among these systems.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The degree to which jamming constitutes one sharply defined transition across different material classes remains debated."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
